ed  the idea of mass media and entertainment  being used to placate a control a  population  turn left fires a Pompey waters of Mars  newer than the end of time all tackled  the idea of one person's value against  the greater good in some fashion or  another dialect the empty child and  arguably most of series one is dealing  with the  impact and unseen consequences of war  both on those who fought it and those  who were caught in the wake of it and  that's not even getting into the  casualness with which the show handled  interracial relationships and the  ominous sexual jack harkness but okay  okay look the show does not begin and  end in 2005 with new who we've got the  classic era so maybe it is the classic  era of Doctor Who that is back when  things were fun and not politically  charged oh hang on  monster peloton featured a mining strike  and was broadcast at a time when mining  strikes were happening in Britain its  precursor curse a peloton had the planet  dealing with whether or not to enter a  Galactic Federation which was again a  very topical in blatant allegory to the  then card debate as to whether or not  Britain should enter into the European  Economic Community the green death is a  pollution will kill us all story the Sun  makers is a vicious jab at taxation  written by a man who just gone through a  really bad tax experience the happiness  patrol features a parody of Margaret  Thatcher who was prime minister at the  time the Cybermen are all about  unchecked technological advancement at  the cost of humanity the epic the war  games is all about the value of  intervention is immerses the doctrine of  non-interference the demons features the  master masquerading as a religious  figure whose hypnotizing his followers  that's just the stuff that I could latch  on to and I don't have nearly the level  of knowledge on the classic era Doctor  Who that I have on knew who but surely  somewhere in the history of the show  there had to have been a time where it  wasn't delivering some political message  that must have been the case at one  point and to be fair it was and that  period of no of her political statements  lasted one story four episodes in about  100 minutes because the second story  ever done back in 1963 was the Daleks  and the Daleks are Nazis that's not  suppositions  that's not speculation that's not modern  reinterpretation Dalek creator Terry  nation was  very upfront and blatant about the  influence of Nazis on the creation of  the Daleks this was important to him to  the point that he made very certain in  genesis of the Daleks that when we see  the Cal edge which is the race that will  eventually be mutated and become the  Daleks before they're even in the metal  casing tanks they are in military garb  and behaving in a fashion that is  reminiscent of Nazis the doctors most  iconic foes there since the second story  ever broadcast were deliberately created  as a science fiction take on a real-life  military presence and political party so  the idea that doctor who has only  recently become politically charged is  simply without merit this show since the  beginning has repeatedly and  consistently made a point of telling  stories that reflect something going on  or that had gone on in the real world  was it all stories no but these are not  outliers it consistently came up over  and over and over again now if you want  to make the argument that you don't like  the political points that the show is  making lately that's fair enough but you  need to own up that that's what your  problem is  well you what you can't do is you can't  hide behind this idea that the show used  to not be political at all but now it is  and that's your problem  own up to the fact that it's not the  presence of the politics but the  specific political beliefs themselves  that you take issue with because this  show has always been a platform for  political ideas and if we are being  honest by and large progressive and  liberal leaning ideas now if you've been  a fan since childhood it is a distinct  possibility that when you first started  watching the show you didn't recognize  the political themes you didn't know  enough about the outside world and what  was going on in politics to draw the  connections and to see them I know that  discovers like that has been the case  for me for all sorts of stuff that I've  loved since I was a kid I revisit as  whoa there's this whole other thing  going on that I didn't even recognize  but not noticing them because you  weren't politically tuned enough to  recognize that connections doesn't mean  that they weren't there so stop making  the argument that the show used to not  be political and now is and that's what  you're hung up about if you don't like  the specific politics being pushed talk  about that make that argument if you  feel that the show used to handle  political topics with more grace and  subtlety than it currently does then  make that argument I don't personally  believe that's the case but I'm willing  to listen if that's the argument you're  prepared to make but to say that you  wish the show wasn't political at all is  to say you wish the show wasn't about  anything except spaceships and lasers  but if the show was stripped of its  political ideas it wouldn't even be  recognizable as Doctor Who so many  elements of what is fundamental to this  show to this character will be gone  there'd be no hoon  there be no Cybermen there'd be no  Daleks heck I would argue there wouldn't  even be a doctor not as we know the  character over the course of this show  the doctor has been many many things  including but not limited to an  interventionist a revolutionary an  anarchist and a pacifist these are all  political ideals these are who the  doctor is this is what the show is so  stop making an argument that simply has  no merit again if you want to tell me  that the specific political message is  being pushed you don't like tell me that  and we'll talk about that but to make  this claim that the show is pushing  politics when it didn't use to is simply  intellectually dishonest it's not true  don't make that argument because it has  no basis make the argument that you're  afraid to make the argument that  actually has you explain why the  specific political views being pushed  you are not okay with or why you are not  okay with the specific means in which  they're being pushed you can't argue  against their simple presence because  they've always been present  political views are in the core and then  the DNA of this show and that happens  since the beginning  dr. who is a political show it always  has been and it should continue to be so  that's my word on this particular topic  what are your thoughts whatever they are  if you can keep them civil please drop  them down the comments let's talk about  it don't forget to like subscribe check  me out on Twitter a council of geeks  give a listen to the council of geeks  podcast available on iTunes and stitcher  and until next time this council is  adjourned  [Applause]  [Applause]
 

